course: dictionary
lesson: 2800
title: The prefix dis- and disrespect
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Disrespect is built from two parts: dis- and respect. The prefix dis- means not or the opposite, so disrespect means not showing respect. Once you know the parts, you can work out a new word like disagree (not agree) or dislike (not like).
explain: Disrespect can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, it is rude behaviour that shows you do not value or care about someone or something. Look at the phrases «show disrespect» and «treat with disrespect»: the word is the thing being shown or given.
explain: Context tells you how people feel when they use the word. «No disrespect intended» means "I do not mean to be rude", and people say it before they say something that might sound critical. The words around the phrase show the speaker is trying to be polite.
fact: Disrespect means rude behaviour that shows you do not value or care about someone or something.
fact: As a verb, to disrespect someone is to treat them rudely or without respect.
fact: The prefix dis- means not or the opposite, as in disagree and dislike.
fact: The slang «dis» or «diss» is short for disrespect and means to insult someone.
exercise: Which word has the prefix dis- meaning not or the opposite? | *disagree | prehistoric | bicycle | rewrite
exercise: People say «no disrespect intended» before saying something critical. What do they want you to know? | *They do not mean to be rude | They want you to show more respect | They are about to insult you on purpose | They have forgotten something
exercise: The prefix in disrespect means: | three | *not or the opposite | before | again
test: Mia says «dis» is short for disrespect. What does dis mean in slang? | To hug someone warmly | *To insult someone | To thank someone | To be late
test: A teacher says, «Treating classmates with disrespect breaks our rules.» What does disrespect mean here? | *Rude behaviour that shows you do not value someone | Sharing your lunch | Being very tall | Singing loudly
exam: Which sentence uses disrespect as a verb, meaning to treat someone rudely? | No disrespect intended, but your drawing is messy | *Ben disrespected his grandma by ignoring her when she spoke | Disrespect is a rule we follow in class | The guest showed disrespect by ignoring the host
